    "collapsible_menu_V8LbeE": {
      "type": "collapsible_menu",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_tab_hEww4i": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "1. How does UraGuard® Shield work?",
            "content": "<p>Here’s what happens when you use the shield:</p><ul><li>The shield liner is placed inside your incontinence brief or diaper, positioned directly under the urethra.</li><li>During the day, urine and stool are absorbed into the incontinence product, creating a warm, moist environment that allows bacteria to multiply and thrive. </li><li>When bacteria build up in this damp space, they may enter the urethra, increasing the risk of urinary discomfort and UTIs.</li><li>UraGuard<strong>®</strong> creates a targeted physical barrier over the urethral area, separating it from the moist parts of the incontinence product where bacteria are present.</li><li>As the urethra is covered, bacteria held in the pad or brief don’t reach the urethral opening, reducing the chances of infection.</li></ul>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_VHbXcc": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "2. How is UraGuard® Shield Different From a Pad?",
            "content": "<p>Unlike full-length pads, UraGuard<strong>® </strong>is a small, targeted shield designed specifically to cover the urethral area — not absorb fluid. It works alongside your existing incontinence brief or disposable underwear.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_3tn3G9": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "3. Is UraGuard® gentle on sensitive skin?",
            "content": "<p>Yes! UraGuard® shields are made with soft, skin-friendly materials chosen with sensitive skin in mind. If you experience any irritation, discontinue use and speak with your healthcare provider.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_SizeFit": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "4. What size is UraGuard® Shield? Will it fit my brief?",
            "content": "<p>UraGuard® is a small, targeted shield — noticeably more compact than a full-length pad. That’s by design: it only needs to cover the urethral area, where protection matters most.</p><p>It’s thin and flexible, and designed to fit inside any standard incontinence brief, diaper, or disposable underwear without adding bulk. Many first-time customers are surprised by how small it is — the compact size is what keeps it discreet and comfortable all day.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_j7GmEL": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "5. How discreet is UraGuard® Shield under clothing? Will it show or feel bulky?",
            "content": "<p>UraGuard® is designed to be completely discreet. </p><p>It’s thin, flexible, and sits inside your existing brief or disposable underwear, so it won’t change how your clothing fits or feel bulky.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_Uqt9RJ": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "6. Does UraGuard® work for men?",
            "content": "<p>UraGuard® is specifically engineered for women, as its design and placement are optimized for the female anatomy. </p><p>While men can use it for incontinence management, the UraGuard® technology may not provide the same benefits. We are actively developing a version tailored for men — stay tuned!</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_NNDXVp": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "7. Is UraGuard® available as a pull-up or tabbed diaper?",
            "content": "<p>Not yet. UraGuard® is currently available as a shield insert, so you can add barrier protection to any incontinence product you already use. </p><p>However, we understand the need for an all-in-one solution, and we’re actively exploring pull-up and tabbed-style options. Stay tuned for updates!</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_4DUM3d": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "8. Does UraGuard® offer a satisfaction guarantee?",
            "content": "<p>Yes! We stand behind the quality of our products. If you’re not completely satisfied, <a href=\"https://www.athenauraguard.com/pages/contact\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">contact our customer support team</span></a> within 30 days for a hassle-free refund or exchange.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_WLjtEA": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "9. Where is UraGuard® made?",
            "content": "<p>UraGuard® is proudly manufactured in the USA. We’re committed to high-quality manufacturing standards to ensure our products meet the needs of women seeking comfort, protection, and urinary health support.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
